WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.180
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar reminding you to Mind Your Decisions

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.840
The International Mathematical Olympiad, or IMO for short,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.020
is an annual competition for pre-college students.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:21.020
More than 100 countries participate and each country sends a team of its 6 elite Math competitors.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.900
On the first day, students solve 3 questions in 4 1/2 hours,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.000
and on the second day, they solve another 3 questions in 4 1/2 hours.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:35.189
Each problem is worth 7 points for a total of 42 points

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.580
In 2019, the individual mean score was about 16 points,

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.900
but there were students who got a perfect paper with 42 points.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.120
This problem comes from day 1 question 1:

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.800
Let Z be the set of integers:

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:00.520
Determine all functions f going from Z to Z, such that for all integers a and b

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:07.588
f(2a) + 2f(b) = f(f(a+b)).

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.620
Now while this is an incredibly challenging problem for most of us,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:19.720
about 60% of these competitors scored a perfect 7 points on this problem.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.300
For them, this was an easy problem,

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.660
but for the rest of us, this is a very challenging problem,

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.560
and in this video, I want to give some indication of how you can solve it.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.620
Pause the video if you'd like to give it a try,

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.840
and when you're ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:49.860
[Theme Music]

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.340
So I'll admit I wasn't able to solve this problem myself, 

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.180
so I want to thank the Art of Problem Solving community,

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.640
Beni Bogoşel's blog,

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.700
and the RedPig YouTube Channel.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:05.120
I read solutions on these places, and it helped me understand how to present it for you.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.500
So how can we solve for all functions over the integers, such that this equality is true.

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:16.119
Now solving this problem is a little bit like giving directions from point A to point B,

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:23.100
you're gonna have to calculate a lot of different routes, until you figure out a good way to go from A to B.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.900
Just like a GPS will show you the shortest path or a path that's easier to understand,

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.620
I'm going to just present the solution to you, as if we've already done all the experimentation

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.180
There may be other easier ways,

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:40.880
but this is just one way that I hope you'll understand. So we'll get started by trying some special values:

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.480
Suppose a = 0:

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.740
we'll take this equation and we'll substitute in a = 0.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:53.820
We get f(0) + 2f(b) = f(f(0+b)).

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.260
0+b simplifies to be b.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.860
Next, we'll consider that this is true for all integers b.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:08.060
Therefore we can substitute the variable x here, and say it's true for all integers x

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.800
Now let's try the special value a = 1,

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:17.470
so we take our identity and then substitute a = 1.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:23.100
1+b will be b+1 because addition is commutative.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:30.040
We're now going to take this f(f(b+1)) and simplify it. How can we do that?

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:35.349
Well, look at our first identity. We have a composition of f(f(x)).

00:03:35.349 --> 00:03:39.699
So we substitute in b+1 wherever we see x.

00:03:39.889 --> 00:03:44.019
And we end up with f(0)+2f(b+1).

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.700
So this will become another identity.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.540
Now recall that this is true for all integers b.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.680
So we'll substitute x here, and we'll just write that it's true for all integers x

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.660
Now we're going to manipulate this equation:

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:05.200
We have a x term on the left and a constant term on the right. So we'll switch them to the other side,

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.119
We'll bring the constant term to the left side, and the x term to the right side

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.300
Now we'll divide both sides of this equation by 2,

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:23.080
Notice the right-hand side of the equation, will be the difference of consecutive terms. This is f(x+1)-f(x).

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:31.360
The left-hand side of the equation will be the value of the f(2) - f(0) all divided by 2.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:36.980
Therefore this will be a constant value and it's true for all integers x,

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.920
This means we have an arithmetic progression,

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:45.420
because the difference of consecutive terms will be some constant value,

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:50.500
This means f(x) can be written as the linear equation:

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.140
mx+n.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.560
We now take this form and substitute it back into the original equation,

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.600
We start with f(2a),

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.200
then we go to 2f(b),

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.430
and finally we have a composition. So first let's do f(a+b),

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:13.480
Then let's do another evaluation of the function.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.680
When we do that we end up with the following equation,

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:23.280
We simplify both sides, and now how are we going to figure out m and n?

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:27.860
We're going to match coefficients of like terms,

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:31.720
so here we have the term a+b on the left, and a+b on the right,

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.640
and this has to be true for all integers a and b.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:39.600
The only way this is true is if we match the coefficients 2m and m²

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.220
Now we also match the constant terms.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:46.740
So we have 3n=mn+n.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.240
We have a system of equations.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.880
We're going to solve this by considering each case.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.040
So how do we solve 2m=m²?

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.620
Well one solution is m=0,

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.080
We're going to substitute that into our second equation.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.260
We have 3n=n and that's only true if n=0.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.760
The other possibility is that m=2,

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:15.940
and in this case, we substitute it in and get 3n=3n, so n can be any integer.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.220
And we now have two possibilities for our solution,

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.720
one will be f(x)=0, and

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:28.960
the other is that f(x)=2x+n for some integer n in Z.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:35.980
We want to verify that these actually are true and substitute them back into our original equation.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.600
We can do that and we'll see that we'll get equality for both cases.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:47.240
Therefore these are the only solutions either f(x) is identically 0.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:52.380
Or f(x)=2x+n for some constant n.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:57.040
I hope this video gave you some sense of how to solve an Olympiad problem,

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.460
and I hope it gave you some idea of how challenging these problems are,

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:05.560
because the competitors found this problem to be on the 'easy side'.

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:11.500
Thanks for watching and for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.780
Thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

